    <description xmlns:py="http://codespeak.net/lxml/objectify/pytype" py:pytype="str">&lt;H1&gt;Disclaimer&lt;/H1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We cannot guarantee the accuracy of the outputs produced by this tool, because accuracy varies globally according to the available datasets and the processing steps applied.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;THIS DATA IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES 
OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS 
BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Elevation and other geospatial datasets may have been modified, clipped, resampled, reprojected, combined, or otherwise processed for use in this map. The original data providers do not endorse this product and are not responsible for any modifications, analysis, interpretation, or conclusions made from the data.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;H1&gt;Data sources/software&lt;/H1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This mapping package is possible thanks to multiple products and services listed below with their corresponding attribution statements.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Elevation data&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This map used terrain data from Mapzen Terrain Tiles / terraincache.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NASA / USGS SRTM. Attribution: SRTM terrain data courtesy of NASA and the U.S. Geological Survey. Approximate/native resolution: about 30 m. Date/acquisition info: SRTM mission 2000. SRTM is used when no higher-resolution local elevation source is available for the area. If you know of a higher-resolution digital elevation model that could improve future maps, please contact us with the dataset details.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;USGS GMTED2010. Attribution: GMTED2010 terrain data courtesy of the U.S. Geological Survey. Approximate/native resolution: about 250 m, 500 m, or 1 km depending on the source product. Date/acquisition info: 2010-11-17. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;small&gt;Raw source raster references reported by terraincache:&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;small&gt;srtm/N21E081.tif&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;small&gt;gmted/10N060E_20101117_gmted_mea075.tif&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;small&gt;Mapzen source families are inferred from the terraincache X-Imagery-Sources metadata. Resolution and date are source-level values unless the filename itself contains a date.&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;HYDROSHEDS - &lt;a href='https://www.hydrosheds.org'&gt;https://www.hydrosheds.org&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This product incorporates data from the HydroSHEDS database which is &amp;copy; World Wildlife Fund, Inc. (2006-2013) and has been used herein 
under license. WWF has not evaluated the data as altered and incorporated within this product, and therefore gives no warranty regarding 
its accuracy, completeness, currency or suitability for any particular purpose. 
Portions of the HydroSHEDS database incorporate data which are the intellectual property rights of &amp;copy; USGS (2006-2008), 
NASA (2000-2005), ESRI (1992-1998), CIAT (2004-2006), UNEP-WCMC (1993), WWF (2004), Commonwealth of Australia (2007), 
and Her Royal Majesty and the British Crown and are used under license. The HydroSHEDS database and more information 
are available at http://www.hydrosheds.org.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;NASA POWER Project Data Sets - &lt;a href='https://power.larc.nasa.gov'&gt;https://power.larc.nasa.gov&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This data was obtained from the NASA Langley Research Center (LaRC) POWER Project funded through the NASA Earth Science/Applied Science Program. It is licensed as Public Domain. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;GDAL - &lt;a href='https://gdal.org'&gt;https://gdal.org&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GDAL/OGR contributors (2020). GDAL/OGR Geospatial Data Abstraction software Library. Open Source Geospatial Foundation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;SAGA GIS - &lt;a href='http://www.saga-gis.org'&gt;http://www.saga-gis.org&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Conrad, O., Bechtel, B., Bock, M., Dietrich, H., Fischer, E., Gerlitz, L., Wehberg, J., Wichmann, V., and Böhner, J. (2015): System for Automated Geoscientific Analyses (SAGA) v. 2.1.4, Geosci. Model Dev., 8, 1991-2007, doi:10.5194/gmd-8-1991-2015.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Mapzen Terrain Tiles - &lt;a href='https://www.mapzen.com'&gt;https://www.mapzen.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ArcticDEM terrain data DEM(s) were created from DigitalGlobe, Inc., imagery and
  funded under National Science Foundation awards 1043681, 1559691, and 1542736;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt; Australia terrain data  &amp;copy; Commonwealth of Australia (Geoscience Australia) 2017;
&lt;li&gt; Austria terrain data &amp;copy; offene Daten Österreichs – Digitales Geländemodell (DGM)
  Österreich;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt; Canada terrain data contains information licensed under the Open Government
  Licence – Canada;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt; Europe terrain data produced using Copernicus data and information funded by the
  European Union - EU-DEM layers;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt; Global ETOPO1 terrain data U.S. National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt; Mexico terrain data source: INEGI, Continental relief, 2016;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt; New Zealand terrain data Copyright 2011 Crown copyright (c) Land Information New
  Zealand and the New Zealand Government (All rights reserved);&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt; Norway terrain data &amp;copy; Kartverket;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt; United Kingdom terrain data &amp;copy; Environment Agency copyright and/or database right
  2015. All rights reserved;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt; United States 3DEP (formerly NED) and global GMTED2010 and SRTM terrain data
  courtesy of the U.S. Geological Survey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
